            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty: update 1988.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>770-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report updates the current indications, techniques and investigational devices used in a busy interventional cardiology practice. Specific attention is devoted toward the problem areas of thrombolytic treatment of acute myocardial infarction, restenosis after angioplasty and the use of angioplasty in the treatment of multivessel coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
